Originally from www.github.com/JaKooLit — Hyprland-Dots v2.2.2, since migrated
from hyprlang to the Lua configuration introduced in Hyprland 0.55.

1.) These files are managed by Nix. They are copied into ~/.config/hypr from
    modules/desktop/hyprland/assets/hypr in the nix config repo, so editing
    them in place only lasts until the next rebuild. Edit the repo instead.

2.) Every file here is a Lua module loaded by ../hyprland.lua via require().
    Each require() is an isolated error scope: a syntax error in one file does
    not stop the others from loading. Emergency binds (SUPER+Q/R/M) remain
    available if hyprland.lua itself fails.

3.) Do not rename these files without also updating the require() list in
    ../hyprland.lua, and the scripts that read them by name:
      - ../UserScripts/QuickEdit.sh      (menu of files to edit)
      - ../scripts/SwitchKeyboardLayout.sh (greps kb_layout from user-settings.lua)

4.) Always check a change before rebuilding:
      Hyprland --verify-config -c ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua
    This validates far more than syntax: unknown option keys, wrong value
    types, invalid keysyms, and bad dispatcher arguments are all reported.
    Caveat: bind option tables ({ locked = true }) are not validated, so a
    typo'd option name is silently ignored.

5.) Guidance on keybinds: avoid assigning a keybind that already exists in
    configs/keybinds.lua, else the two will conflict. Prefer adding
    { description = "..." } to new binds — `hyprctl binds` exposes it and
    ../scripts/KeyBinds.sh renders it.

6.) Colours are not defined here. ../wallust/colors.lua is generated from
    config.jvf.theme.colors and swapped at runtime by jvf-theme-switch.
